Z||000004||Ronnie||09-26-2001||10:55 PM||||Just a couple of notes of thanks here. I wanted to thank David Hunter for the ignition module that he let me have when mine died. And also , thank Ed Parks for doing all the work of putting that thing in for me with a HOT engine. I know he burned his hands working on that thing several times.<BR>Also , I had to make David take some money in payment back at the Motel for the ignition module. He just told me to get one and then have it with me in case next time someone else needed one. That's what makes the Fiero community what it is. Bunch of nice guys always willing to help others. THANKS!!!!<P>------------------<BR>88GT auto,88Formula T-Top,86GT 4spd<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_sig_new_paint_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000005||Wolfhound||09-27-2001||05:21 AM||||Good shots, the tunnel especially. I drove through one by Braille.<BR>After we left the second stop there was a Med Red GT that had gone ahead and waited at an overlook to video the line of Fieros coming through a long sweeping inside curve. I sure would like to see that video. Anyone know who it was?<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||09-27-2001||09:23 AM||||I'm pretty sure it was the guy with the silver 3.4 turbo GT. Forgot his name. I would pay to have that video.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroHarry||09-30-2001||04:11 PM||||All who attend RFTH come away with awe inspiring veiws.<BR>The gentle reminder of the good life away from city dwelling-hustle and bustle!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00233.jpg"> <P>Soaring high above the clouds on the winged stallion, my soul finds freedom!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00225.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||1
